PyTorch 2.x compatibility for the pinned TargetDiff submodule.

torch.load() defaults to weights_only=True from PyTorch 2.6 onward, which
rejects TargetDiff's checkpoint: it pickles an EasyDict training-config object
alongside the tensors, not a bare state dict. sample_for_pocket.py is the
entrypoint the orchestrator's TargetDiff backend calls, so it must opt back
into the full unpickler. The checkpoint is our own mirrored, trusted file
(huggingface.co/vladsft/agent-harness-weights), so weights_only=False is safe.

This patch is only needed by the Blackwell / cu128 local env (PyTorch 2.8);
it is harmless on the cu117 Docker env (PyTorch 1.13 ignores the kwarg's
modern default, and accepts it as an explicit argument).

Applied by scripts/apply_targetdiff_patches.sh (idempotent).

--- a/scripts/sample_for_pocket.py
+++ b/scripts/sample_for_pocket.py
@@ -49,7 +49,7 @@
     misc.seed_all(config.sample.seed)

     # Load checkpoint
-    ckpt = torch.load(config.model.checkpoint, map_location=args.device)
+    ckpt = torch.load(config.model.checkpoint, map_location=args.device, weights_only=False)
     logger.info(f"Training Config: {ckpt['config']}")

     # Transforms
